/target/
# Scratch directories some crate tests create beside their manifest.
/hosts/*/target/
/clients/*/target/
/.idea/
/.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.tmp
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# macOS bundles now build into dist/macos/; these cover older checkouts and
# worktrees whose scripts still write them to the repository root.
Arcen Deck.app/
Arcen Pier.app/
Arcen Agent Helper.app/
.gstack/
# Local key material. Never commit.
/keys/
# Support bundles copied from hosts hold logs, configuration and host
# identity. Never commit.
/support/
# Provisioning profiles contain sensitive team credentials — store outside git or in AppleCerts/
# The rule is deliberately unanchored: the Pier has its own profile now, and a
# path-specific pattern only protects the one directory someone thought of.
*.provisionprofile

# Release artefacts assembled by hand; binaries are never committed.
dist/*
!dist/README.md

# Retired installer output directory; installers now go to dist/<platform>/.
/dist-installers/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local working material that is never committed.
#
# Anything that names real infrastructure, accounts or credentials belongs in
# an ignored path, not in tracked files: test-host inventories, notary profile
# names, certificate common names, signing private keys, deployment runbooks.
# The signing procedure is documented in docs/operations/macos-signing.md;
# only the values stay local. Ignored paths are not backed up by git.
#
# .github/ is deliberately NOT ignored: release.yml and workflows/ are
# functional configuration that GitHub reads from the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.local/
*.private.md
